  "solution": {
    "text": "Coagulating power  <math><mo>∝</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mtext> value</mtext></mrow></mfrac><mo>∝</mo><mtext>charge</mtext></math> <br/><br/>As  <math><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></math>  is a positive sol so negative ion will cause the coagulation.<br/><br/>Ions of the given electrolytes are,  <math><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msubsup></math>  and  <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math> .<br/><br/>As  <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math>  has minimum charge thus has maximum coagulating value.",
